    <string name="background_help_title">Keep Accessibility running when leaving the app</string>
    <string name="background_help_reason">On some phones, swiping away the app or clearing recent apps may force-stop Auto Scroll and turn off its Accessibility service.</string>
    <string name="background_help_steps">1. In Auto Scroll app settings, allow background activity and auto-launch if available.\n2. Lock Auto Scroll in recent apps if your phone supports it.\n3. Use Home instead of swiping away the app when you want to keep using the floating controls.</string>
    <string name="background_help_recovery">If Accessibility was turned off, reopen Auto Scroll and enable its service again in Accessibility settings. The app cannot grant this permission itself. Background options vary by manufacturer; these settings do not guarantee the service will remain active.</string>
